Q: Azure Blob upload using SAS URL fails with TypeError: Failed to fetch due to Content Security Policy (CSP) in ASP.NET WebForms A: <p>Ok let's focus on your HTTP Web Server config:</p>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;system.webServer&gt;
  &lt;httpProtocol&gt;
    &lt;customHeaders&gt;
      &lt;add name=&quot;Content-Security-Policy&quot;
           value=&quot;default-src 'self' https://apps.itl.co.tz/broker/;
                  connect-src 'self' https://dbatchattachmentsuat.blob.core.windows.net;&quot; /&gt;
    &lt;/customHeaders&gt;
  &lt;/httpProtocol&gt;
&lt;/system.webServer&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Don't use whitespace in the value here. You have a semicolon, then tabs or whitespace separating connect-src. In XML this can result in unintended values being passed to the client browser. Use a single line, such as this (and don't use path or trailing slash in default-src either:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;add name=&quot;Content-Security-Policy&quot;
           value=&quot;default-src 'self' https://apps.itl.co.tz; connect-src 'self' https://dbatchattachmentsuat.blob.core.windows.net;&quot; /&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>I'm also assuming, given your CORS policy using localhost, that you are testing this out on your app deployed to localhost. Remember that CORS will block requests if this App is running anywhere other than https://localhost:44380, so if so, you need to add the origin which the user is browsing to.</p>
